mfortably. Its 2027 capex is up 12%, so debt looks workable for it. I found no evidence that Pellham Power has issued or lined up replacement debt.\n- **Equity:** Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short. Two utility share offerings were also cut back in size. Equity can't be counted on right now.\n- **Pellham's plan:** Its 2027 capex is up 18%. It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\". That suggests it can't fund the full plan.\n- **Why Pellham can't use debt instead:** I infer leverage or rating limits are the reason. The documents don't state this.\n- **Implication for grid equipment:** Pellham's 2027 orders will probably fall even though its stated capex rises. The planned 18% increase overstates what will be spent.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no data on leverage, credit ratings, or the size of either company's funding gap. The debt view rests on one Norvane bond. The Pellham view rests on its own actions.\n\nThis summarises the two sub-judgments, debt (n5.r1) and equity (n6.r1).","ttft_ms":2241,"type":"result","duration_ms":28009,"uuid":"f317f9d7-80a3-47c5-baee-6c56ad164706","ttft_stream_ms":1543,"time_to_request_ms":566,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":112,"system_prompt":20,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":70,"input_hooks":27,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":14,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":65,"init_frame_send":21,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":27,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":78,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":9,"tool_schema_build":17,"message_normalization":20,"client_creation":30,"request_build":46},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":333,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":83,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":173,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":98,"process_rss_mib_result":188,"process_anon_m